WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.780
- Today's video is
sponsored by Skillshare,

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.460
so warm thank you to the
whole Skillshare team

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.240
to supporting the work on
my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.070
In the past, I worked for
six years at McKinsey,

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.750
but before that, I also
spent about half a year

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.850
at the IT consulting firm, Accenture.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.900
So in this video, I wanna
contrast these two experiences.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.090
I will talk about what the
differences and similarities are

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.570
of working in an MBB consulting firm

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.080
and of working in a IT consulting firm.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.030
Now, I do not wanna make
this about any specific firm,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.350
So while, of course,
this video is influenced

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.750
by my experiences at
McKinsey and at Accenture,

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.050
I also talked to other people working

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.730
at other consulting
firms in these two groups

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.850
to make sure you have
a well-rounded picture

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:42.683
of all of this.

00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:44.990
And, of course, I need to make
the caveat in the beginning

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:48.140
that while I'm generalizing
now a little bit in this video,

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.990
of course, projects within one firm

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:51.930
can be very different from each other,

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.460
firms which in the IT consulting

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:57.380
or MBB sector can be quite different,

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:58.333
so, of course, take this
with a grain of salt,

00:01:00.155 --> 00:01:01.610
but I do believe that this can give you

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.050
a good and solid understanding

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.140
of what the differences
are, and of course,

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:08.290
I hope that this can also
inform your career decisions,

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:12.340
and help you understand what
you actually want for yourself

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.270
if you are thinking about joining a firm

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.700
in each of these two groups.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.460
So while I come to another coffee break

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.080
on my channel, Firm Learning,

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.940
hope you all had a good
start to the new year.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.030
On my channel, Firm Learning,

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.160
I want to help you to become successful

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.370
in the first years of your career,

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:30.760
talking about topics like
career communication,

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.690
management, consulting, personal finance,

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.430
and other related things to that.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.500
So without further ado,
let's jump into it,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.480
and today I wanna talk
about five distinct areas

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.120
of similarities and differences,

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.050
and these are the team size,
the duration of projects,

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:46.850
the type of work that you do,

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.630
the background of your colleagues,

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.640
and of course, the whole work/life balance

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.180
and lifestyle aspect of it as well.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:53.720
So let's start by the team size,

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:54.590
because I do believe

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.940
that this is one of the most
significant differences,

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:59.650
because on average, the team size

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:02.430
in these IT consulting
projects is much larger.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.490
Again this will differ,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.910
and you find deviations for
that in both directions,

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.780
but at an MBB firm, the typical team size

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:12.200
is two to five people,
including the project lead,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.350
so as a consultant, you are
one of two to five people

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:16.183
on the team.

00:02:16.183 --> 00:02:18.180
This is very different than working

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.360
on a large IT consulting project,

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.970
which can easily have 20, 30,
40, 50 people, or even more,

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.620
on the senior consulting team.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.770
So for instance, you might
work on an SAP implementation,

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:32.080
so a project where your help your client

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.860
to implement a new ERP
system, such as SAP,

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.780
within their own organization
and with their own teams.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.470
So the plus of working
in such a large team

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.093
in IT consulting is, of course,

00:02:43.093 --> 00:02:44.400
that you have the opportunity

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.120
to talk to many of your colleagues.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:46.953
Maybe there are some

00:02:46.953 --> 00:02:48.870
with whom you don't get along that well,

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.280
but then you would still have plenty

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.700
of other people to choose from

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.800
with whom you can bond,
from whom you can learn,

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.440
and then maybe also do
some things together

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.273
in your free time.

00:02:56.273 --> 00:02:57.660
But of course this also means

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.300
that often, your responsibility
in the whole project

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.010
will be a bit smaller compared
to these smaller teams.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.070
If you're one of 30, one of
40, one of 50 people, of course

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:10.310
the type of tasks that you
will do will be quite different

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.770
because indeed, at a typical MBB project,

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.680
you are one of only two, three
or four people on the team,

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.620
so you will, from the very beginning,

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.860
have a crucial role on that team.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.220
If you do not get the work done,

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.410
the team does not have
enough slack, usually,

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:27.450
to just pick up your work,
do your work for you.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.870
This is not how it works.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:31.890
And of course, there's more
room like that in a larger team.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.820
So this leads me to my second point,

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:37.260
and this is the duration
of such a typical project,

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.820
and here the main difference is

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.570
that the projects in IT consulting

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.540
often go considerably longer than in MBB.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.320
So a typical MBB project
will be three to five months.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.260
There are also projects which
only go a couple of weeks.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.560
The shortest project that
I worked at at McKinsey

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.040
was only for two weeks.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.190
And yes, there are also
projects which go longer,

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.550
but then there is the
understanding that you're released

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:01.280
after six, seven month,
maybe eight month, latest,

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.300
that then you will roll off the project,

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.620
and then some other
consultant will roll on

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.660
and take your spot.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.540
This is different from IT consulting,

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.480
and especially in these large
implementation projects,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.820
you can easily be stuck
for one or even two years

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.460
on a specific project.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:18.900
There, this culture of
rolling off the project

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.610
after only a couple of month
is not really established

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.630
And of course there's also client pressure

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:26.310
to have the consultants
on the team for longer,

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.890
because of course, over time,

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:29.790
the consultants will get experience,

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.460
will learn the intrinsics
of a specific company,

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:34.480
So, of course, the client is pushing

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.770
for keeping the consultant
on the team longer,

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.170
and then this is exactly what will happen

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.230
in these typical large IT
implementation projects.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:43.740
So if you join consulting

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.150
because you want to see
lots of different things

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.950
in a short amount of time,

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.490
I believe that the value proposition

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.810
of these MBB projects is much larger,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.270
much more valuable to you.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.410
Of course, the advantage
of being on these projects

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.510
that go really longer,
for one or two years,

00:04:57.510 --> 00:04:58.640
is that you can really build

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.670
much deeper client relationships.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:01.570
You have the opportunity

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.830
to really see something being implemented

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.000
from the conceptualization
in the beginning

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.350
up until the point that the whole system,

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:09.400
the thing that you're implementing,

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.800
is really going live, is really working.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:13.300
Of course, this can give you

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.550
a tremendous sense of achievement,

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.600
a tremendous sense of accomplishment,

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:20.950
which maybe you don't experience
that way on an MBB project

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.760
because very often, you
leave after the strategy,

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.540
after the concept has been developed,

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.870
and then it's up to the organization,

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:28.160
or maybe another consulting team,

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.580
to then do the implementation.

