00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:50.950
And now this indeed leads

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:52.920
to the third aspect I wanna talk about,

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.300
and this is the type of work
that you will be tasked with.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:59.160
On such a big IT project, of course,

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.420
your work will be much more hands-on.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.190
You might work with Big Data cubes

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:04.760
that you help the client setting up

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.110
in order to then build a BI,

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.550
a business information system,

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:09.490
to help the client analyze its data.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:13.120
Or you might migrate data
from one system to the other

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.920
in order then to really make the migration

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.460
to a new ERP or SAP system, for instance.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.760
You might dig deep into the
processes of the client,

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.457
really mapping out all these processes

00:07:21.457 --> 00:07:22.980
and then translating them

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.040
into an IT system that
the client is using.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.260
Overall, the work will
be much more oriented

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:30.370
towards implementation, towards
getting these things done.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:33.300
And this, of course, can be
contrasted to work at MBB,

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.880
but it's much more theoretical, right?

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.790
You often develop concepts, strategies.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:38.657
The end result of your work

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:40.650
will typically not be a running IT system

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:43.250
but rather a document, maybe
a PowerPoint presentation.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.820
And here is where times
are changing a bit.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:49.050
Now also MBB is doing some of
these other things as well.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:50.930
Now I'm also already
foreseeing all the comments

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:53.050
from the IT consulting
guys that will tell me

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:53.950
that of course, in IT consulting,

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.540
you do these conceptual tasks as well.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.520
So yes, all of this is correct,

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.270
but if you talk about the
tendencies, the directions,

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.410
I do think that this
distinction is very relative.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:04.500
And this is actually something

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.670
that I found very
interesting and inspiring

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.030
when I worked at Accenture
in IT consulting,

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:09.863
because of course,

00:08:09.863 --> 00:08:12.130
on these large IT implementation projects,

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.730
you will often work together
with computer scientists,

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.830
with people that really
do the implementation,

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.400
that can code, that
can set up the systems.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.890
The way that these people
work and think about things

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.270
of course is quite different

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.740
from the typical consultant
that you might sit together

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.700
in a team room, in an MBB project.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.060
So probably, the profiles
of the people you work with

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:31.510
are a bit more heterogeneous,

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.130
and I did found this very enriching.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.140
Of course, the backgrounds
of the people you work with

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.170
are quite different at MBB as well,

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.230
but I think it's fair to say

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:40.810
that the mindset of these
people, the whole way of working,

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:42.180
was a bit more homogeneous

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.687
than what I found in IT consulting.

00:08:43.687 --> 00:08:45.890
But of course, the upside
of working together

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:48.590
with these people at MBB
is that because, allegedly,

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:52.430
MBB have the most selective
consulting recruiting processes,

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:55.480
you really get to meet
extremely inspirational,

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.430
extremely ambitious,
extremely driven people

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.130
in these MBB consulting firms,

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:02.640
so while their profiles might
be a bit more homogeneous,

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.080
you can trust that the
learning that you will get

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.000
out of working with these
people will be insane,

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.550
and this of course is a huge plus

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:10.980
for working at an MBB firm.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.740
And the fifth point I wanna
talk about is the lifestyle.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.270
So first of all the similarities.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:17.910
So both IT consulting and MBB consulting

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:21.180
share this lifestyle of
traveling to the client,

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:24.010
being at the client
from Monday to Thursday,

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:26.190
and then usually having an office Friday,

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:27.840
and then more or less a free weekend.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.080
So these are the
similarities you can expect

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.750
that usually, again on
average, and again I know

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:35.270
that this might change
also, project by project,

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.280
usually, the lifestyle
will be a bit better

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.210
in IT consulting.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.010
So from my very personal experiences,

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.280
usually people were
leaving the client site

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:44.880
at around 7:00 p.m.,
sometimes even earlier,

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.240
and if we stayed at the
client until 8:00 p.m,

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:49.000
this was already a long day.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.100
And also once the people
left the client site

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.440
and worked from the hotel,

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.720
I didn't really perceive the culture

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.610
of then still continuing
to work in your hotel room,

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.250
continuing to work in the evening.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:00.540
And this is of course very different

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:01.990
from what you need to expect

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:05.230
if you work at an MBB firm,
like McKinsey, BCG, or Bain.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.710
If you want to learn more about that,

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.890
check out the video that I did

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.950
about a typical work week
at an MBB consulting firm.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.610
So what you will clearly see there is

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:13.880
that what you can expect is

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.870
that you really need to work much longer,

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:18.260
so usually, if you're
completely done at 10:00 p.m,

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.020
this will be considered a good day,

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.550
and there will be many days where you work

